<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zand dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zand Empire, Zands, Zand</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zand dynasty ruled much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> from about 1751 to 1794, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karim-khan-zand">Karim Khan Zand</a>, a chief of the Zand tribe of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a>. Karim Khan governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> under the title of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vakil">Vakil</a>, bringing a period of relative peace after the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a>. After his death in 1779 the dynasty was weakened by succession disputes and was destroyed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajars</a>, who captured and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lotf-ali-khan">Lotf Ali Khan</a> in 1794.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty.jpg" alt="Zand dynasty" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aliasgharnadafi messi1 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%B4%DB%8C%D8%B1_%D9%88_%D8%AE%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%B4%DB%8C%D8%AF_%D8%A8%D8%AF%D9%88%D9%86_%D8%B4%D9%85%D8%B4%DB%8C%D8%B1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
